# Verify ↔ CI parity (mandatory)

Live CI is the gate. Verify must use the **same argv** as live CI on the
**pinned Python** (see `.python-version` — currently **3.11**).

## Live CI commands (do not invent softer variants)

Inspect (read-only): `git show HEAD:.github/workflows/ci.yml`

On Python **3.11** (the repo pin):

```bash
pip install -e ".[dev]"
ruff check .
ruff format --check .
mypy src tests
pytest -n auto -m "not slow and not docs" --cov=blueberries_voi --cov-branch \
  --cov-report=term-missing --cov-report=xml --cov-fail-under=80
```

## Hard rules for **verify**

- Use **`ruff format --check .`**, never treat mutating `ruff format .` as the gate.
- Run the full gate block above on **Python 3.11** before writing
  `.team/qa/T-XXX.md` PASS. A different local interpreter is not PASS.
- Prefer the **pip** install path CI uses; `uv sync` alone can hide unlocked-pip
  drift.
- Reviewers do **not** run these tools; they cannot catch format/mypy misses.
- Agents must **not** edit `.github/workflows/`; if live CI YAML must change,
  give the human one copy-paste command only.

## Note (numpy / mypy)

`[tool.mypy] python_version = "3.11"` matches the pin. If you temporarily use
Python ≥ 3.12 (e.g. packaging / Pyodide checks), **numpy ≥ 2.5** stubs can fail
mypy with `Type statement is only supported in Python 3.12 and greater` inside
`numpy/__init__.pyi`. That is outside the single-version CI gate; fix in-repo if
you need those interpreters, do not weaken CI.
